{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>At all times</b> — Let a man love his friend, and a brother loves at the time of trouble that is born, and does not love at all times." "<b>Is born</b> — It ought to be תולד, like: ובא עליך רעה (and trouble comes upon you)." "<b>A man, loves</b> — [verses 18–19] Two verses joined. That is, a man who clasps hands to become a guarantor before his friend the lender, he is called lacking heart, and he loves to do it, on account of transgression and strife that his friend will stir up against him."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {2 "Reading מצה as connected to the root of מצה/מצות (strife, contention); the precise form is unusual."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:23:23.309558293Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}